WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.467
The Pentagon

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.501
says an Iranian made

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.636
drone killed an American contractor

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.838
and wounded five U.S.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:05.538
service members

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.341
after it struck a base in northeast

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.876
Syria.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.011
President Joe Biden

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.313
responding with airstrikes against groups

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.381
affiliated with Iran's

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.949
Revolutionary Guard in Syria.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.417
And you can see ambulances

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.552
rushing to that scene in what looks like

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.821
a burning building off to the side.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.690
The US still has roughly 900

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.291
troops on the ground in Syria to help

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.726
stamp out ISIS.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.627
Just yesterday,

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.763
their commander testifying to Congress

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.465
about how Iran is using proxy militias

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.366
to attack

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.200
American soldiers

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.902
with drones and rockets.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.137
So let's go to our national security

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.371
reporter, Natasha Bertrand.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:38.872
She joins us

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.106
live at the Pentagon Natasha,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:40.907
good morning to you.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.308
This breaking overnight, the U.S.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.477
military says it's ready to respond

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.812
not just to this,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.747
but to any additional Iranian attacks

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.449
if this continues to escalate

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.284
That's right, Poppy.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.952
And Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.721
did issue a statement last night saying

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.089
that he authorized the strike

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.157
after President Biden

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.792
ordered it in response

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.527
to a series of attacks

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.095
by these of groups

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.063
affiliated with Iran's

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.164
Revolutionary Guard Corps

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.599
against US personnel in Syria.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.901
This is not the first time

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.202
that the US has conducted

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.203
these kinds of strikes,

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.204
but it is

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:11.538
these

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.573
these kinds of attacks are

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.908
increasing and the US says

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.009
that it's going to respond

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.178
in a proportional way.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.850
President Joe Biden ordering a U.S.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.086
airstrike in eastern Syria Thursday

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:26.753
after U.S.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.620
intelligence assessed

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.922
that an Iranian origin

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.424
drone killed an American contractor

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.026
and wounded five U.S.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.594
service members and another U.S.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.662
contractor.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.996
Biden authorized the strike,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.065
quote, against facilities used by groups

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.767
affiliated with Iran's Islamic

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.001
Revolutionary Guard Corps.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.269
Secretary of Defense Lloyd

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.971
Austin said in a statement.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.573
The Department of Defense said it, quote,

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.808
took proportionate and deliberate action

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.810
intended to limit the risk of escalation

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.212
and minimize casualties.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.047
The U.S.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.616
military maintains approximately 900 U.S.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.884
troops in Syria.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.318
Some of

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:58.852
which are there

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.187
as part of a coalition to defeat ISIS.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.755
But those forces are often

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.791
under attack by Iranian proxies.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.659
Iran's vast

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.795
and deeply resourced proxy forces

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.997
spread instability throughout the region

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.832
and threaten our regional partners.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:13.800
The commander of U.S.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.501
Central Command

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.268
said in a statement

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.269
following the strike, quote,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.371
We are postured for scalable options

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:18.872
in the face

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.940
of any additional Iranian attacks.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.876
Testifying on Capitol Hill

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.010
Thursday, Chiarelli said that

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.944
Iranian proxies

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.312
have carried out attacks on U.S.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.213
forces in the Middle East.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.550
78 times since the beginning of 20, 21.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.086
And so what Iran does to hide its hand

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.487
is they use Iranian proxies.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.089
That's that's either UAV

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.790
or or rockets to be able

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.026
to attack our forces in Iraq or Syria.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.063
Are these considered acts of war by Iran?

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.099
They are being done

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:46.399
by the

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.934
Iranian proxies, is what I would tell

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.135
you, Congressman.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.503
The Biden administration has carried out

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.205
multiple airstrikes against militias

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.573
affiliated with Iran

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.208
following previous attacks on U.S.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.210
facilities in the region.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.077
Biden's first known

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:58.845
military action

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.847
was a strike in February 2021

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.649
after rocket attacks on U.S.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.517
troops in Iraq.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.020
Now, adding to this concern is yet

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.787
another thing

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.589
that Khairallah, the commander of U.S.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.423
Central Command,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.791
told Congress last week,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.159
which is that today

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.127
Iran possesses

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.628
the largest and most diverse

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.263
missile arsenal in the Middle East,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.231
with thousands

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.133
of ballistic and cruise missiles.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:20.733
And we should note

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.168
that two of those wounded

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.303
service members

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.871
from the strike on Thursday

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.172
were treated on site.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.041
But three additional service members

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.642
and a US contractor

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.277
were actually medically evacuated,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.513
evacuated to coalition medical facilities

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.081
in Iraq Poppy. Don.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.316
Really significant overnight.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.650
Natasha, thank you very much for that.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.851
Reporting from the Pentagon.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.652
Don, thank you.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:43.022
We're very lucky to have our military

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.923
analyst and retired

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:44.857
Air Force Colonel Cedric

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.159
Leighton to walk us through that.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.327
Colonel, thank you so much.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.828
Listen, to the first strike

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.231
happening in the northeast

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.265
and then just south of

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.601
that is where Biden authorized

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.135
that strike back again.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.103
Can you tell us what happened

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.273
Yeah, John, good morning.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.442
So we're basically with the first strike

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.643
that the Iranians

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.012
conducted, the Iranian proxies conducted,

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.447
I should say.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.716
What we're looking at here is

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.518
in the northeastern part of Syria.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.019
The U.S.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.687
maintains a major presence

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.556
with Kurdish forces.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:19.459
So this is a vestige of the work

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.894
that we did against ISIS to destroy that

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.663
that entity.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.497
And, of course,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.633
there's still elements that exist there

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.267
What happened

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.302
was the strike occurred on the U.S.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:30.169
facility,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.972
and that ended up killing the contractor

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.341
and wounding the five soldiers

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.076
and the other contractor

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.779
So with that IED, that

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.081
the Iranian proxies are working

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.717
very much in conjunction with Iran.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.386
And it's also something to note

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.021
that when you look at the way

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.856
in which this happened,

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.090
you can see this happening

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.526
right after Iran and Saudi Arabia.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.962
Much of the relationship

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.030
with China is felt.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.098
So there is a lot that's going on here.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.033
A lot to unpack.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:03.303
But the basic idea is that the U.S.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.172
then responded after this strike occurred

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.776
and the were on the map that you have by

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:10.743
you doing

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.813
that was where that Iranian group

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.214
was actually located.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.550
So the attack that the US conducted

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.084
was right

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.252
there more or less

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.287
in the central part of the country.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.322
Are you expecting the U.S.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.090
military to respond further?

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:28.061
I think this is it for the moment.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.263
But what would happen

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.198
if the Iranian proxies did

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.833
to move forward

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:34.967
with some other attacks,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.602
then you can expect that Central Command,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:36.936
the U.S.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:37.870
Central Command,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.872
would be responding in kind.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.940
So they've basically said

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.775
that they would use proportionate force.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.077
Any time that something like

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:44.877
this happened

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.012
and this is the response

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.948
after about 80 attacks that have occurred

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.984
since the beginning of 2021,

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.820
as we've been reporting, they saw U.S.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.554
personnel there.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:54.954
The U.S.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:55.621
Intel says that

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.589
the strike was carried out

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.990
by these Iranian proxies

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.292
that you mentioned in the region.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.627
What more do we know about where they are

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.063
and the threat that they pose to the U.S.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.198
military, to the U.S.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.332
personnel?

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:07.533
Right.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:10.069
So most of these groups are located

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.204
in the eastern

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.705
and central parts of Syria.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.173
There are some that are located

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.309
in the western part of the country.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:17.276
A lot of the fighting

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.878
that was going on

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.381
in the Aleppo region, for example, I

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.616
Iranian proxies were involved in that

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.618
in these Syrian war.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:28.621
So these elements are really throughout

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.922
the country of Syria.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.959
And they can turn and attack any forces

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.160
where the side

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.295
is, the Syrian defense forces,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:37.997
democratic forces

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.566
that are aligned with us over the Kurds

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.469
or some other entity, including the U.S.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.004
forces that are there.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.739
Just last Thursday, the top U.S.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.607
military general

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.341
for the Middle East

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.643
testified before Congress

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.012
that Iran is significantly more

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.580
military capable than ever.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.314
Let's listen and then

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.449
I'll get your response. It is

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.419
today, Iran is

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.421
exponentially more capable than they were

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.723
just five years ago today.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:04.557
Iran possesses

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:05.958
the largest and most diverse

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.994
missile arsenal in the Middle East.

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.128
Thousands of ballistic

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:09.529
and cruise

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:10.329
missiles,

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.130
many capable

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.332
of striking anywhere in the Middle East.

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.700
Iran also maintains

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.301
the largest

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:17.403
and most capable UAV force in the region.

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.939
So Iranian proxies

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.808
have carried out attacks on U.S.

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.342
forces in the Middle East.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.311
78 times since the beginning of 20.

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:26.312
21.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.514
What are you concerns, Colonel?

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.716
So what this show is, is that

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.885
there's a real proliferation of arms

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:33.753
in the Middle East.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:36.322
And Iran is been culprit in this case.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.590
And what they are doing in order

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.825
to protect

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:39.559
the identity

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:40.693
of who's doing this,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.862
at least protected initially

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:44.697
is to give a lot of these weapons

00:07:44.697 --> 00:07:45.832
to proxy forces

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:47.133
so that they can use what's called

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.701
plausible deniability.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.168
In other words,

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.169
they can wash their hands

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.304
of whatever happened

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:52.205
and say it wasn't done.

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:54.240
So even though it really was them.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.708
So this is very concerning

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:58.244
because it really directly impacts

00:07:58.478 --> 00:07:59.645
American interests

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.447
anywhere in the Middle East.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:02.615
It really impacts

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:03.749
the ability of the Kurds,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.952
for example, to maintain

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.154
a relative peace in their region.

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.822
And it puts at risk

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:11.657
any type of peace agreement

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:14.393
that was reached in the Syrian civil war.

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:15.928
So this is something

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:16.863
that is very dangerous

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.531
and could explode it in.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:20.132
Yeah, that is Cedric

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.367
Leighton, Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.235
A little bit later on,

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:23.169
we're going to have John Kirby.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:23.803
He's going to join us

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:25.104
from the White House. Thank you, Colonel.

